# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the root of the deployed directory; `public/`
# is copied there verbatim by the build.
#
# `no-transform` is the whole point. Cloudflare rewrites HTML at the edge --
# JavaScript Detections injects an inline <script> into every page it serves --
# and the policy in `src/csp.ts` allows no inline script, so the browser blocks
# it and reports a violation on a page that asked for none of it. `no-transform`
# is the response saying the body is to be served as it was built.
#
# The rest of the value is what Pages sends for HTML by default, restated
# because naming the header here replaces it.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
